{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Moses rose up, and Joshua his minister</b> — I do not know what Joshua's role was here. And I say that the disciple was accompanying his teacher up to the place of the boundary of the mountain, beyond which it was not permitted to go, and from there \"and Moses went up alone to Elohim,\" while Joshua pitched his tent there for all forty days, for so we find that when Moses came down, \"and Joshua heard the voice of the people in shouting\" (Exodus 32:17) — we learn from this that Joshua was not among them. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 24:13). And in my opinion Joshua was among the seventy elders, for there are not in Israel seventy elders worthy of proximity to Elohim more than he, and when Moses separated from them, he would accompany his teacher up to the boundary. And do not press me with the statement of our Sages concerning the punishment of those elders at Taberah (Tanhuma, Beha'alotkha 16), for they would say this about all of them except Joshua, because he was worthy of divine visions and all prophecy:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:47.036107185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}